## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F2 | open | BLOCKING | js/common/developmentModeAdaptive.js | 🚨 blocking crap ratchet failure red ci — removestaleappendix measured crap 10 threshold 8 the rework hunks that fixed the file delete contract commit 3881e5ec6 pushed this function over the repo s crap ratchet both failed crap checks on this head report the same measurement ci failures md crap job — runs 43191214482 43191091107 crap ratchet new 8 js common developmentmodeadaptive js removestaleappendix 10 0 regression s 1 new over threshold 0 improvement s 0 removed error process completed with exit code 2 the unit suite itself is green 9799 passed 0 failed in the same job — the break is pure complexity growth the existence probe two try catch blocks the compound if existed result result deleted true all landed in one function cc 10 at 100 coverage ⇒ crap 10 fix — decompose into helpers the exact discipline this pr s sibling module already documents js common developmentmodeplan js appendixoverridepath split so every function stays under the crap threshold the same file s thresholdsetting resolvethresholds follow it keep the probe before the delete reading after deletion would always report missing javascript readability probe true when the appendix file exists unreadable ⇒ assume stale function staleappendixexists io var read io io file read file read try return typeof read path developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path string catch e return true delete the appendix contained — the platform returns deleted bool and never throws function deletestaleappendix io var remove io io file delete file delete try return remove path developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path catch e return null defensive only — the platform does not throw function removestaleappendix io var existed staleappendixexists io var result deletestaleappendix io if existed result result deleted true console warn could not remove the stale plan mode appendix at developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path developmentmode describerawvalue result behavior tests and the documented warning contract stay byte identical — only the crap number crosses back under the ratchet the existing three failure shape tests pin all three helpers paths this does not re open the resolved file delete thread — the fix itself is correct and stays only its complexity is over the measured gate |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: 3881e5ec6b4e492a5a1ec9b8ffe2e529d0386804
Current head: d43ccb91235c38a4195b1f24900411b3a2bac913

